# Floor invariant 16 of 16 (spec/floor-v2.md §4). Layer: floor.
# Statement carries the floor prose verbatim.
"@context": "https://yeetz.dev/bedrock/context/v1"
"@id": "https://yeetz.dev/bedrock/vertex/invariant-16-agents-md-register"
"@type": "https://yeetz.dev/bedrock/ontology/Invariant"
label: "AGENTS.md is the resident situation graph"
layer: "floor"
statement: >
  AGENTS.md is the resident situation graph: one generated TriG working-set
  projection, injected into every agent context by the harness. `situation/`
  is the complete canonical store and every source validates; definition,
  architecture, current risks, Decisions, and compact routing faces for
  active Plans are resident. Draft, done, and abandoned Plans, episodic
  records, references, and every body stay cold behind disclosed paths.
  Never hand-edit AGENTS.md; always regenerate it. After work changes
  reality, re-situate it — emit knowledge, never rules.
